{"id": "swebq0115", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.0, "n_chunks": 2, "n_concurrent": 2, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1737, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "Canada;Australia;Kingdom of Great Britain;United States of America;United Kingdom;Ireland;New Zealand", "query": "what countries speak english natively?", "transcript": "Which countries speak English natively?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Countries where English is spoken natively by a large share of the population include the United States, the United Kingdom, Canada, Australia, New Zealand, and Ireland. It's also widely spoken in places like South Africa, Singapore, Jamaica, and several Caribbean nations. So if you're learning English as a second language, knowing these countries can be helpful!", "expert_answer": "Countries where English is spoken natively by a large share of the population include:\n\n- United States\n- United Kingdom\n- Canada\n- Australia\n- New Zealand\n- Ireland\n\nEnglish is also a native language for many people in countries and territories such as:\n\n- South Africa\n- Singapore\n- Jamaica\n- Trinidad and Tobago\n- Barbados\n- Bahamas\n- Belize\n- Guyana\n- Antigua and Barbuda\n- Saint Kitts and Nevis\n- Saint Lucia\n- Saint Vincent and the Grenadines\n- Grenada\n- Dominica\n\nNote: Many other countries use English as an official or second language, but it is not necessarily spoken natively by most of the population.", "expert_latency_s": 3.55, "stall_ms": 22, "relay_ms": 1561}
