{"id": "swebq0124", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.32, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2784, "eot_read_ms": 19, "reference_answer": "Northern Mariana Islands;Norfolk Island;Guam;American Samoa;New Caledonia;Marshall Islands;Kiribati;Nauru;Fiji;Cook Islands", "query": "what countries have territories in oceania?", "transcript": "What countries have territories in Oceania?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Several countries have territory in Oceania.  Australia, New Zealand, and Papua New Guinea are sovereign states located there.  Other Pacific island nations like Fiji, Samoa, and Vanuatu also fall within the region.  In addition to these independent nations, some countries maintain overseas territories in Oceania, such as the United States with Hawaii and American Samoa, France with French Polynesia and New Caledonia, and the United Kingdom with Pitcairn Islands.", "expert_answer": "Countries with territory in Oceania include:\n\n**Sovereign states in Oceania**\n- Australia\n- New Zealand\n- Papua New Guinea\n- Fiji\n- Solomon Islands\n- Vanuatu\n- Samoa\n- Tonga\n- Tuvalu\n- Kiribati\n- Nauru\n- Palau\n- Marshall Islands\n- Federated States of Micronesia\n\n**Countries with overseas territories or parts in Oceania**\n- United States — Hawaii, Guam, American Samoa, Northern Mariana Islands, etc.\n- France — French Polynesia, New Caledonia, Wallis and Futuna\n- United Kingdom — Pitcairn Islands\n- Chile — Easter Island / Rapa Nui\n- Indonesia — western New Guinea is often considered part of Oceania/Melanesia\n- New Zealand — Tokelau; also associated states Cook Islands and Niue\n\nDefinitions vary, especially regarding Indonesia, Hawaii, and some Pacific islands.", "expert_latency_s": 10.84, "stall_ms": 21, "relay_ms": 2114}
