{"id": "swebq0136", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.69, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.0937, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "Croatian language;Bosnian language;Serbian language", "query": "what language do people from bosnia speak?", "transcript": "What language do people from Bosnia speak?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "People from Bosnia and Herzegovina commonly speak **Bosnian, Serbian, and Croatian**. These are mutually intelligible standard varieties of the same South Slavic language continuum, and which name people use often reflects ethnic, cultural, or political identity.", "expert_answer": "People from Bosnia and Herzegovina commonly speak **Bosnian, Serbian, and Croatian**. These are mutually intelligible standard varieties of the same South Slavic language continuum, and which name people use often reflects ethnic, cultural, or political identity.", "expert_latency_s": 1.9, "stall_ms": 24, "relay_ms": 1182}
{"id": "swebq0139", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 1.62, "n_chunks": 2, "n_concurrent": 2, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2147, "eot_read_ms": 19, "reference_answer": "San Jose Municipal Rose Garden;The Tech Museum of Innovation;Winchester Mystery House;Japantown;Downtown San Jose;Rosicrucian Egyptian Museum;San Jose Museum of Quilts & Textiles;San Jose Museum of Art;Alum Rock Park;Santana Row", "query": "what to do san jose ca?", "transcript": "What to do San Joseca?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "If you're looking for things to do in San Jose, there's plenty to choose from depending on your interests. For a unique experience, the Winchester Mystery House is a must-see with its fascinating architecture. If you're into science and tech, The Tech Interactive offers some great hands-on exhibits. For shopping and dining, Santana Row has a lively atmosphere, while the San Pedro Square Market is perfect for foodies or just enjoying some live music. If you want something more relaxing, the Municipal Rose Garden is beautiful and free to visit. There are also museums like the Rosicrucian Egyptian Museum and family-friendly spots like Happy Hollow Park & Zoo. Let me know what you enjoy—whether it's outdoor activities, nightlife, or exploring local culture—and I can help narrow it down!", "expert_answer": "If you mean **San Jose, CA**, here are good things to do:\n\n- **Winchester Mystery House** – famous historic mansion with odd architecture  \n- **The Tech Interactive** – hands-on science and technology museum  \n- **Santana Row** – shopping, dining, and nightlife  \n- **San Pedro Square Market** – food hall, bars, live music  \n- **Municipal Rose Garden** – beautiful free park, great for photos  \n- **Rosicrucian Egyptian Museum** – unique museum with Egyptian artifacts  \n- **Happy Hollow Park & Zoo** – good for families/kids  \n- **SAP Center** – Sharks hockey, concerts, events  \n- **Alum Rock Park** – hiking and nature  \n- **Downtown San Jose** – restaurants, bars, museums, and events\n\nIf you tell me your interests—food, nightlife, hiking, family activities, or budget—I can suggest a more specific plan.", "expert_latency_s": 5.98, "stall_ms": 23, "relay_ms": 3859}
{"id": "swebq0142", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.14, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1913, "eot_read_ms": 19, "reference_answer": "Lorenzo de' Medici;Domenico Ghirlandaio;Giovanni Pico della Mirandola;Girolamo Savonarola;Melozzo da Forlì", "query": "what inspired michelangelo buonarroti?", "transcript": "What inspired Michelangelo Buonarroti?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Michelangelo Buonarroti was inspired by several major sources including classical Greek and Roman art, the human body which he studied deeply through anatomy, Christian faith and biblical themes especially in works like the Sistine Chapel ceiling, Renaissance humanism emphasizing human potential, earlier artists such as Donatello and Giotto, his teacher Domenico Ghirlandaio, and the intellectual culture of the Medici circle in Florence.", "expert_answer": "Michelangelo Buonarroti was inspired by several major sources:\n\n- **Classical Greek and Roman art**, especially ancient sculpture and ideals of heroic beauty.\n- **The human body**, which he studied through anatomy and portrayed with great power and realism.\n- **Christian faith and biblical themes**, especially in works like the *Sistine Chapel ceiling* and *The Last Judgment*.\n- **Renaissance humanism**, which emphasized human potential, dignity, and creativity.\n- **Earlier artists**, including **Donatello**, **Giotto**, and his teacher **Domenico Ghirlandaio**.\n- **The Medici circle in Florence**, where he encountered philosophy, poetry, and Neoplatonic ideas.\n\nIn short, Michelangelo was inspired by ancient art, human anatomy, religion, and the intellectual culture of Renaissance Florence.", "expert_latency_s": 4.02, "stall_ms": 21, "relay_ms": 1922}
{"id": "swebq0145", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 1.72, "n_chunks": 2, "n_concurrent": 2, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.4618, "eot_read_ms": 19, "reference_answer": "\"\"\"After Hitler's coup in 1933, Goebbels was named \"\"Reich Minister for Public Enlightenment and Propaganda\"\" and president of the newly-formed \"\"Chamber of Culture\"\", which gave him total control over Germany's media.\"\"\"", "query": "what was goebbels role?", "transcript": "What was Goebbels' role?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Joseph Goebbels was the Nazi Party’s chief propagandist and served as Minister of Propaganda in Nazi Germany from 1933 to 1945. He controlled the press, radio, film, and public messaging to promote Hitler, spread Nazi ideology, and incite antisemitism. In the final days of the regime, he briefly became Chancellor of Germany after Hitler’s death.", "expert_answer": "Joseph Goebbels was the Nazi Party’s chief propagandist and served as Minister of Propaganda in Nazi Germany from 1933 to 1945. He controlled the press, radio, film, and public messaging to promote Hitler, spread Nazi ideology, and incite antisemitism. In the final days of the regime, he briefly became Chancellor of Germany after Hitler’s death.", "expert_latency_s": 3.38, "stall_ms": 23, "relay_ms": 1894}
{"id": "swebq0148", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.46, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1464, "eot_read_ms": 19, "reference_answer": "Spanish Language", "query": "what languages do they speak in costa rica?", "transcript": "What languages do they speak in Costa Rica?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "In Costa Rica, the main language is Spanish. There are also some other languages spoken there, like English in tourist areas and a few indigenous languages on the Caribbean coast.", "expert_answer": "In Costa Rica, the main and official language is **Spanish**.\n\nOther languages spoken include:\n\n- **English**, especially in tourism and by some communities on the Caribbean coast  \n- **Costa Rican Creole English / Mekatelyu**, mainly in Limón Province  \n- Indigenous languages such as **Bribri**, **Cabécar**, **Maléku**, **Ngäbere**, and **Buglere**  \n\nBut for most everyday situations, **Spanish** is the language used throughout the country.", "expert_latency_s": 3.3, "stall_ms": 24, "relay_ms": 786}
