{"id": "swebq0166", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 1.44, "n_chunks": 2, "n_concurrent": 2, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2128, "eot_read_ms": 19, "reference_answer": "Orville Wright;Wilbur Wright", "query": "who were wright brothers?", "transcript": "Who are Wright brothers?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "The Wright brothers were Orville and Wilbur Wright, American aviation pioneers who invented and built the world's first successful powered airplane. On December 17, 1903, they made history with the first controlled, sustained flight of a powered aircraft near Kitty Hawk, North Carolina.", "expert_answer": "The Wright brothers were **Orville Wright (1871–1948)** and **Wilbur Wright (1867–1912)**, American aviation pioneers credited with inventing and building the world’s first successful powered airplane.\n\nOn **December 17, 1903**, near **Kitty Hawk, North Carolina**, they made the first controlled, sustained flight of a powered, heavier-than-air aircraft, called the **Wright Flyer**.", "expert_latency_s": 3.13, "stall_ms": 20, "relay_ms": 1269}
