{"id": "swebq0196", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.18, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2857, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "Pacific Time Zone;UTC-8", "query": "when do they change the time in california?", "transcript": "When do they change the time in California?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Got it! In California, they change the time for Daylight Saving Time twice a year. In spring, clocks move forward one hour on the second Sunday of March at 2 a.m., and in fall, they move back one hour on the first Sunday of November at 2 a.m. So next time that happens is on November 1st, 2026, when we'll set our clocks back an hour.", "expert_answer": "In California, clocks change for Daylight Saving Time:\n\n- **Spring forward:** **Second Sunday in March** at **2:00 AM** → clocks move to **3:00 AM**\n- **Fall back:** **First Sunday in November** at **2:00 AM** → clocks move back to **1:00 AM**\n\nThe next change is **Sunday, November 1, 2026**, when clocks **fall back one hour**.", "expert_latency_s": 4.34, "stall_ms": 23, "relay_ms": 1908}
{"id": "swebq0199", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 1.81, "n_chunks": 2, "n_concurrent": 2, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1492, "eot_read_ms": 19, "reference_answer": "Édouard Manet;Paul Cézanne;Henri Rousseau;Paul Gauguin;Sara Murphy;Diego Velázquez;Jean Auguste Dominique Ingres;Eugène Delacroix;Alfred Jarry;Francisco Goya", "query": "who influenced picasso art?", "transcript": "Who influenced Picasso?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Picasso was influenced by many artists and traditions, especially Paul Cézanne, whose work helped shape his Cubism style. He was also inspired by African tribal art and Iberian sculpture, which can be seen in some of his early masterpieces like Les Demoiselles d'Avignon. Other important influences include El Greco for his dramatic figures, Henri de Toulouse-Lautrec for Parisian subjects, and the color and expressive styles of Gauguin and Van Gogh. Later on, he worked closely with Georges Braque to develop Cubism even further.", "expert_answer": "Picasso was influenced by many artists and traditions, especially:\n\n- **Paul Cézanne** — major influence on Cubism and geometric form  \n- **African tribal art** and **Iberian sculpture** — influenced works like *Les Demoiselles d’Avignon*  \n- **El Greco** — dramatic figures and expressive style  \n- **Henri de Toulouse-Lautrec** — early Parisian subjects and style  \n- **Paul Gauguin** and **Vincent van Gogh** — color and expressive distortion  \n- **Jean-Auguste-Dominique Ingres** — classical line and figure drawing  \n- **Georges Braque** — close collaborator in developing Cubism  \n\nThe strongest influences are usually considered **Cézanne**, **African/Iberian art**, and **Braque** in relation to Picasso’s development of Cubism.", "expert_latency_s": 5.13, "stall_ms": 20, "relay_ms": 2819}
{"id": "swebq0202", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.6, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.4483, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "Kohler", "query": "where are kohler sinks manufactured?", "transcript": "Where are Kohler sinks manufactured?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Kohler sinks are manufactured in several places around the world, depending on the model. Some of their products come from Kohler, Wisconsin, but others may be made in countries like China or Mexico. To know exactly where a specific sink was made, you can check the product label or look up its details online.", "expert_answer": "Kohler sinks are manufactured in multiple locations worldwide, depending on the model and material. Some Kohler sinks—especially enameled cast iron products—are made in Kohler, Wisconsin, USA, while other models may be produced in countries such as China, India, or Mexico.\n\nFor the exact origin of a specific sink, check the product packaging, label, or Kohler’s specification sheet for that model.", "expert_latency_s": 6.75, "stall_ms": 23, "relay_ms": 1369}
{"id": "swebq0205", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.6, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1522, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "Knowing;Triangle;The Hunger Games;The Expendables 2;The Last Song;Timeless;Empire State;The Hunger Games: Catching Fire;Arabian Nights;Love and Honor", "query": "what movies has liam hemsworth played in?", "transcript": "What movies has Liam Hemsworth played in?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Liam Hemsworth has appeared in movies including Knowing, Triangle, The Last Song, The Hunger Games, The Expendables 2, Love and Honor, Empire State, Paranoia, The Hunger Games sequels, Cut Bank, The Dressmaker, Independence Day Resurgence, The Duel, Isn't It Romantic, Killerman, Arkansas, Poker Face, Land of Bad, and Lonely Planet.", "expert_answer": "Liam Hemsworth has appeared in movies including:\n\n- **Knowing** (2009)\n- **Triangle** (2009)\n- **The Last Song** (2010)\n- **The Hunger Games** (2012)\n- **The Expendables 2** (2012)\n- **Love and Honor** (2013)\n- **Empire State** (2013)\n- **Paranoia** (2013)\n- **The Hunger Games: Catching Fire** (2013)\n- **Cut Bank** (2014)\n- **The Hunger Games: Mockingjay – Part 1** (2014)\n- **The Dressmaker** (2015)\n- **The Hunger Games: Mockingjay – Part 2** (2015)\n- **Independence Day: Resurgence** (2016)\n- **The Duel** (2016)\n- **Isn’t It Romantic** (2019)\n- **Killerman** (2019)\n- **Arkansas** (2020)\n- **Poker Face** (2022)\n- **Land of Bad** (2024)\n- **Lonely Planet** (2024)", "expert_latency_s": 9.88, "stall_ms": 22, "relay_ms": 1716}
{"id": "swebq0208", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.41, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2004, "eot_read_ms": 19, "reference_answer": "Fender Stratocaster;Rickenbacker 360/12", "query": "what kind of guitar did george harrison use?", "transcript": "What kind of guitar did George Harrison use?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "George Harrison used many guitars, but he is especially associated with a few iconic ones. He’s known for his Rickenbacker 360, which was great for early Beatles recordings. He also played Gretsch models like the Country Gentleman and Duo Jet during that time. Later on, he had a custom-painted Stratocaster nicknamed \"Rocky,\" plus a famous red Gibson Les Paul called \"Lucy.\" In his solo career, he often turned to a Fender Rosewood Telecaster.", "expert_answer": "George Harrison used many guitars, but he is especially associated with:\n\n- **Rickenbacker 360/12** — a 12-string electric guitar used on early Beatles recordings.\n- **Gretsch Country Gentleman** and **Gretsch Duo Jet** — major early Beatles guitars.\n- **Fender Stratocaster “Rocky”** — his psychedelic-painted Strat.\n- **Gibson Les Paul “Lucy”** — a famous red Les Paul given to him by Eric Clapton.\n- **Fender Rosewood Telecaster** — used during the *Let It Be* era and the rooftop concert.", "expert_latency_s": 4.55, "stall_ms": 24, "relay_ms": 2317}
{"id": "swebq0211", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 1.48, "n_chunks": 2, "n_concurrent": 2, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.3198, "eot_read_ms": 19, "reference_answer": "Tyne and Wear", "query": "what is newcastle metro?", "transcript": "Newcastle Metro.", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "The **Newcastle Metro**, officially the **Tyne and Wear Metro**, is a light rail system that serves several towns around Newcastle upon Tyne in North East England. It opened in 1980 and runs through places like Gateshead, Sunderland, and various areas of Tyneside. It's managed by Nexus and has two main lines often referred to as the Yellow and Green Lines.", "expert_answer": "The **Newcastle Metro**, officially the **Tyne and Wear Metro**, is a light rail/rapid transit system serving **Newcastle upon Tyne, Gateshead, Sunderland, North Tyneside, and South Tyneside** in North East England.\n\nIt opened in **1980** and is operated by **Nexus**. Key stations include **Monument**, **Haymarket**, **Central Station**, **Gateshead**, **Airport**, and **Sunderland**. Its two main lines are commonly shown as the **Yellow Line** and **Green Line**.", "expert_latency_s": 4.33, "stall_ms": 20, "relay_ms": 1738}
