{"id": "swebq0226", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 2.51, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2264, "eot_read_ms": 19, "reference_answer": "Reflecting telescope", "query": "what was sir isaac newton's inventions?", "transcript": "What was Sir Isaac Newton's inventions?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Sir Isaac Newton is best known for these major inventions and discoveries. He invented the reflecting telescope, developed calculus, formulated the laws of motion, and proposed the universal law of gravitation.", "expert_answer": "Sir Isaac Newton is best known for these major inventions and discoveries:\n\n- **Reflecting telescope** (Newtonian telescope) — his main practical invention, built in 1668.\n- **Calculus** — he independently developed a form of calculus, which he called “fluxions.”\n- **Laws of motion** — three fundamental laws describing how objects move.\n- **Universal law of gravitation** — the theory that all masses attract each other.\n- **Optics discoveries** — showed that white light is made of different colors using prisms.\n\nHis most famous actual *invention* was the **reflecting telescope**.", "expert_latency_s": 3.61, "stall_ms": 21, "relay_ms": 795}
